@page "/support"

<PageTitle>Support - Clarity Belongs</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Clarity Belongs support for accounts, follows, monitoring history, and notifications." />
</HeadContent>

<div class="shell public-shell article-shell">
    <header class="hero compact-hero article-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">SUPPORT</div>
        <h1>Help with Clarity.</h1>
        <p class="public-lead">Find answers for setting up follows, understanding status and history, managing your account, and troubleshooting common issues.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="article-body">
        <section>
            <h2>Start here</h2>
            <div class="support-grid">
                <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/how-to-monitor-a-website-for-changes"><strong>Set up your first follow</strong><span>Learn how baseline and history work.</span></a>
                <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/website-change-monitor-vs-uptime-monitor"><strong>Choose the right watch</strong><span>Separate availability from whole-page content changes.</span></a>
                <a class="learn-card" href="/account"><strong>Account</strong><span>Review your current plan and capacity.</span></a>
                <a class="learn-card" href="/settings"><strong>Notification settings</strong><span>Review the notification settings available to your account.</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Common questions</h2>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <details open>
                    <summary>Why is there no change after the first check?</summary>
                    <p>The first successful observation establishes the baseline. Clarity needs a later successful observation to compare against it.</p>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Why did a follow enter Error?</summary>
                    <p>The latest check could not complete successfully. Clarity records the error state and retries according to the follow's schedule.</p>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>Where do notifications appear?</summary>
                    <p>Current launch accounts use in-app notifications in My Clarity. Email delivery is not presented as an available launch feature.</p>
                </details>
                <details>
                    <summary>What targets can Clarity monitor?</summary>
                    <p>Clarity monitors supported public internet targets. Private, local, and otherwise restricted endpoints are blocked.</p>
                </details>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Need help with your account or a problem?</h2>
            <p>Use Contact for account or support questions. Use Product feedback when you want to report an idea, bug, or experience that can help improve Clarity.</p>
            <div class="action-row">
                <a class="button" href="/contact">Contact Clarity</a>
                <a class="button secondary" href="/feedback">Give product feedback</a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </article>
</div>
